        "original_id": "c0e1b0b4-2905-551d-898e-0da51138f283",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elizabeth Wordsworth, Christopher Wordsworth, John Wordsworth, Kathleen Kenyon\n- Organizations: St Hugh's College, Oxford, Anglican Church\n- Roles: Bishop of Lincoln, Bishop of Salisbury, Principal, liturgical scholar\n\nFacts:\n- Christopher Wordsworth was born on 30 October 1807 and died on 20 March 1885.\n- Christopher Wordsworth was an English bishop in the Anglican Church and a man of letters.\n- Elizabeth Wordsworth was the daughter of Christopher Wordsworth, Bishop of Lincoln.\n- Elizabeth Wordsworth was the sister of John Wordsworth, Bishop of Salisbury, and Christopher Wordsworth, a liturgical scholar.\n- St Hugh's College, Oxford was founded in 1886 by Elizabeth Wordsworth as a women's college.\n- Kathleen Kenyon was Principal of St Hugh's College, Oxford from 1962 to 1973.\n- St Hugh's College, Oxford accepted its first male students in its centenary year in 1986.",
